# No spread / rest syntax

Do **not** use JavaScript or PHP **spread or rest** syntax (`...`). It is harder to scan in review and diffs. Use explicit, named alternatives.

## JavaScript / Vue

```javascript
// Bad
const merged = { ...defaults, ...overrides };
fn(...args);

// Good
const merged = Object.assign({}, defaults, overrides);
// or assign fields explicitly:
const merged = { name: overrides.name ?? defaults.name, status: overrides.status ?? defaults.status };

fn(arg1, arg2, arg3);
```

For arrays: `items.concat(extra)`, `Array.prototype.push.apply`, or explicit loops — not `[...a, ...b]`.

## PHP

```php
// Bad
$merged = [...$defaults, ...$overrides];
foo(...$args);

// Good
$merged = array_merge($defaults, $overrides);
foo($arg1, $arg2, $arg3);
```

Unpacking in array literals and argument lists is disallowed unless the user explicitly requests an exception for a specific line.
